  "worked_solution": "We use Taylor's theorem in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{\u2032}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{\u2033}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+\u22ef,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x$ and $a=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)\\,\\,\\,\\, & =\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x \\\\ f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=0 \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(x) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2 \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(x) & =-4\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=0 \\\\ {f}^{\u2034}(x) & =8\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x \\\\ {f}^{\u2034}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x & =0+(-2)(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{(0)}{2!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}+\\frac{(8)}{3!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{3}+\u22ef \\\\  & =-2(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{4}{3}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{3}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
